methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification. The concentrated loading method is appropriate for the training of highly qualified athletes.\" The evidence named: \"distribution of glycolytic work over the annual cycle \nPDF p. 371 PDF pp. 370-371 \n### claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality.md\nchapter: \"6.9.4\"\n# How Long One Emphasis Keeps Paying: Explosive Strength Plateaus in 3-4 Months, Aerobic Fitness in 2-3, Glycolytic Capacity Peaks at About 4\n**What it is** — The authors say the duration of a load \"can easily be miscalculated by the average coach,\" and that besides the overall limit set by the body's current adaptation reserves, \"there is also an upper limit to the duration of using any specialised training means with a primary emphasis, the exceeding of which is detrimental to the development of maximum and explosive strength, as well as to the growth of aerobic and anaerobic capacity. Exceeding this limit does not enhance fitness and wastes the athlete's time and energy\" (PDF p. 370 / printed p. 359, checked against the page imag\nPDF p. 370 PDF p. 372 PDF p. 373 \n### framework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state.md\nchapter: \"6.11\"\n# Three Levels of Change in Fitness State: Long-Term (Volume), Medium-Term (Content), Short-Term (Acute and Largely Random)\n**What it is** — From Sirenko's study and \"other studies of the influence of training loads on functional indicators,\" the authors identify \"three levels of change in an athlete's fitness state during training\" (PDF p. 378 / printed p. 367, checked against the page image):\nPDF p. 378 PDF p. 379 \n### principle--programming-is-an-art-on-principles-not-an-algorithm.md\nchapter: \"6.17\"\n# Programming Is an Art Based on Principles, Not a Rigid Order or an Algorithm; One-Variable Short Studies Mislead It\n**What it is** — The chapter's closing section (PDF p. 403 / printed p. 392, checked against the page image): \"it is unacceptable to understand programming as the following of some instructions which prescribe a rigid order in the organisation of training. Furthermore, it is also senseless to view it as the creation of a precise algorithm, as is done in chess. Programming in sport is an art based on specific principles, which allows the coach creative initiative in making the final decisions.\" The authors call the chapter \"only the first steps,\" and leave to the coach \"the sequence of loading \nPDF p. 379 PDF p. 403 \n### principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue.md\nchapter: \"6.9.4\"\n# Volume Drives Long-Term Adaptation and Prepares Connective Tissue; Intensify Only After Extensive Low-Intensity Work\n**What it is** — The authors give volume two roles. First: \"The function of the volume of the load consists chiefly of the systematic and prolonged disturbance of the body's homeostasis, which stimulates the mobilisation of its energy resources and plastic reserves. This is the fundamental condition for switching from the acute (specific) reaction ... to the general (non-specific) adaptive reaction, and then to the development of long-term adaptation of the body. Therefore, in each successive annual cycle athletes should execute larger volumes of loading (within optimal limits) to raise and ma\nPDF p. 369 PDF p. 370 PDF p. 374 \nls: unrecognized option `--time-style=+%H:%M'\nusage: ls [-@ABCFGHILOPRSTUWXabcdefghiklmnopqrstuvwxy1%,] [--color=when] [-D format] [file ...]\nclaim--ldte-in-endurance-training-documented-only-after-altitude-training.md\nheuristic--within-session-order-of-explosive-means-matters-less-than-volume-and-contrast.md\nheuristic--time-technique-and-competition-strength-work-to-the-ldte-window.md\nframework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state.md\nclaim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes.md\nprinciple--programme-objective-approach-quantified-goals-dictate-training.md\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md\nprinciple--programming-is-an-art-on-principles-not-an-algorithm.md\nframework--four-documents-for-programming-and-controlling-training.md\nframework--eight-weaknesses-of-the-matveyev-model.md\nheuristic--build-the-annual-plan-backwards-from-competitions.md\nheuristic--in-season-stabilisation-twice-weekly-30-minutes.md\nclaim--conversion-phase-is-a-misnomer.md\nheuristic--gpp-and-spp-form-one-unit-curtail-gpp-for-advanced-athletes.md\nframework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap.md\nheuristic--progress-skills-only-at-70-80-percent-technical-reliability.md\nclaim--hettinger-four-features-that-stimulate-strength-gains.md\nclaim--heavy-medium-light-alternation-beats-monotonic-increasing-loading.md\nheuristic--test-monthly-under-constant-conditions-and-compare-with-targets.md\nframework--eight-step-sequence-for-programming-annual-training.md\nheuristic--set-mesocycle-boundaries-by-main-competition-dates.md\nframework--tricyclic-annual-model-for-individual-and-one-on-one-sports.md\nclaim--prolonged-competition-period-volume-cuts-lower-special-work-capacity.md\nprinciple--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue.md\nframework--annual-models-for-medium-and-long-duration-endurance-sports.md\nclaim--middle-distance-runners-need-strength-and-jump-training-benchmarks.md\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md\nframework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md\nheuristic--build-training-theory-from-interacting-complexes-and-coach-scientist-cooperation.md\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md\nheuristic--routine-artificial-restoration-can-blunt-adaptation.md\nframework--intensity-zone-distribution-and-load-recording.md\nframework--matveyev-microcycle-and-mesocycle-types-and-sequences.md\nprinciple--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum.md\nheuristic--sequential-