{"parentUuid":"1a92651b-6573-469a-988c-1b64fb40d146","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeede644703c0347a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffnhALhorTMmw66vuJx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** Of the 16 entries, 5 are GO, 11 need fixes and none is NO-GO. The review is in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md`.\n\n**Required fixes, in one line:**\n1. Fig 6.22 is misread in `four-observations` and `compensatory-adaptation`.\n2. `distributed-vs-concentrated` compares the wrong two quantities, doesn't say the model Issurin criticises is Verkhoshansky's, and wrongly rules it out for medium-level athletes.\n3. `concentrated-blocks` needs its conflict sorted by what each number measures.\n4. Process notes about \"batch 6a\" must come out of `mesocycle` and `bondarchuk`.\n5. The writer's own reasoning needs an \"Inference:\" label in `mesocycle`, `functional-specialisation`, `bondarchuk` and `logical-scheme`.\n6. Small source mismatches: `three-sport-groups` (\"further subdivide\"), `compensatory` (\"taken much further\"), the `vankov` title, `arousal` (curve B and the unsourced introvert/extrovert claim), `logical-scheme` (shaded boxes), and where the Zhurbinoi citation sits in `functional-specialisation`.\n7. Change the PDF 359 locators from \"text layer only\" to \"checked against the page image\".\n\n**Key findings:**\n- **Fig 6.22 (the worst error).** Two entries say graph A is \"nearly straight\" and contradicts the text's parabola, and claim a high-resolution crop check. My 400 dpi crop shows A's rise shrinking every year (about 0.39, 0.25, then 0.11 in slope), which fits the parabola. The contradiction doesn't exist.\n- **Fig 6.23.** Every value used in both panels is right to within about one percentage point. The writer's caution about panel A is fair. In panel B, which curve dips deepest can't be settled because the curves cross. But the \"figure against text\" claim compares how long the dip lasts with how long a block lasts. The text puts the heavy volume in \"the first half of the training phase\", and a dip lasting to weeks 7 to 9 of 18 is exactly that.\n- **Block durations.** `contested` is right, because three numbers measure the same thing (how long a concentrated block lasts): 3-4 weeks (PDF 360), 4-8 weeks (PDF 305) and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381). The others measure different things and are being mixed in:\n  - 4-12 weeks at PDF 305 and 381 is the length of a single-emphasis training stage.\n  - 4-12 weeks at PDF 375 is how long the delayed training effect lasts.\n  - 18-22 weeks is how long it takes to use up the adaptation reserve.\n- **Issurin 2016.** The critique matches the vault summary (p.6 and p.11) and is aimed at the concentrated single-emphasis model. The entry should say that model is Verkhoshansky's.\n- **Borrowed management theory.** All three entries name whose model it is: Yerkes-Dodson, Vroom through Tellier, and Hersey-Blanchard. None presents it as the authors' finding, and `untested` is right for all three.\n- **Eric's baseline.** All 19 cited lines match in quote, line number and tag, including the football energy-system lines 116-117.\n- **PDF 359.** I opened the page image and the text layer matches it for every quote used.\n- **Duplicates.** None found. The report lists four reciprocal-link suggestions and five missing ideas, mostly from the management section (decision-making, management versus leadership, Blake-Mouton grid, needs theories), plus the endurance monitoring point on PDF 359."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11716,"cache_read_input_tokens":215772,"output_tokens":1355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":78},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ep